The program takes no input — it's a fixed self-check driver — so there was no scanf/fgets behavior to model. Structure mirrors the C one file per translation unit:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
- [38;5;10msrc/hashmap.rs[0m — open-addressed map with FNV-1a over the key's native bytes. Generic over a [38;5;10mCopy[0m value with [38;5;10mNone[0m as the [38;5;10mNULL[0m sentinel. Quirks preserved verbatim: [38;5;10mshould_resize[0m counts tombstones, the resize path re-enters [38;5;10mput[0m, and in [38;5;10mput[0m the "reuse deleted slot" branch is tested [3mbefore[23m the key-match branch (so a tombstone ahead of a live key yields a duplicate insert).[0m[0m
- [38;5;10msrc/tree.rs[0m — nodes live in a [38;5;10mVec<TreeNode>[0m arena and the map stores arena indices, which reproduces the C pointer-identity/aliasing semantics without unsafe code. Freed slots are never reused, matching the fact that the C program never observes a recycled node address. [38;5;10mstrncpy[0m NUL-padding, [38;5;10m%s[0m-stops-at-NUL printing, and the sign-losing arithmetic in [38;5;10mcount_descendants[0m/[38;5;10mget_height[0m (a missing child contributes [38;5;10m-1[0m) are all kept as-is.[0m[0m
- [38;5;10msrc/cout.rs[0m — the one non-obvious piece. With stdout on a pipe, glibc fully buffers it while stderr stays unbuffered, so a merged capture shows both [38;5;10mError:[0m lines [3mbefore[23m the banner. Rust's line-buffered stdout would have interleaved differently, so stdout is accumulated in a buffer and flushed once at the end of [38;5;10mmain[0m.[0m[0m
- [38;5;10msrc/main.rs[0m — the test sequence, with [38;5;10massert()[0m → [38;5;10massert!()[0m (both abort on failure). The two expected stderr lines come from the duplicate-ID and max-children tests.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
One translation choice worth flagging: [38;5;10mtest_hashmap_basic[0m compares [38;5;10mhashmap_remove[0m's return against [38;5;10m&val2[0m, a pointer-identity check. I modeled the four stack ints as slots in a small [38;5;10mVec<i32>[0m and compare indices, which preserves the identity semantics rather than value equality.[0m[0m
